WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.920
A CPAC was mostly worthless.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:07.920
The second day was a complete throw away.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.890
Nothing worth covering happened on the second
day Saturday, which is good because I was

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.760
in bed with a fever from my second coronavirus
vaccine dose.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.590
I wouldn't have been able to cover any of
it anyway.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.970
Fortunately, in a sense, there was nothing
worth covering.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:27.470
But one theme that sort of wound its way throughout
Friday and Saturday and Sunday is that CPAC

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:33.820
attendees were unwilling to accept that Donald
Trump lost.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:40.120
We are, what, just a few days short of for
December, January, February, March were days

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:47.420
from being four months beyond the election,
which Joe Biden easily won more easily than

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.600
the margin by which Trump won in 2016.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:57.329
And CPAC speakers, I guess because they're
still sort of kowtowing to Trump, placating

00:00:57.329 --> 00:01:01.089
Trump will not admit that Trump simply lost.

00:01:01.089 --> 00:01:02.719
Let's go through some examples.

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:05.440
Here is Tom Fitton from Judicial Watch.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:12.000
This is one bizarre guy with some kooky ideas
saying Trump had the votes on Election Day,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.860
but vote totals changed as ballots were counted.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.860
Can you imagine?

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.690
Take a listen.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:28.360
On Election Day, President Trump had the votes
to win the presidency.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:34.090
These vote totals were changed because of
unprecedented and extraordinary counting after

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.310
Election Day.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:41.790
Now, in a literal sense, what Tom Fitton says
is true.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:47.670
Votes that were cast by Election Day were
counted after Election Day.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:52.050
Legally, as always, happens with absentee
ballots.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.320
And as those votes were counted, the results
changed.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.420
Yet that is in a technical sense, it is true.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.310
He wants you to believe something illegal
happened.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.670
Of course it didn't.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:08.590
Then Larry Kudlow, Donald Trump's former economic
adviser, talking about polling from last October.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.280
He's put we have ballots that we counted.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.459
Now, you talk about polling beforehand.

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:19.440
But Larry Kudlow is talking about polling
from before the election, comments on that,

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:24.560
I was interested last October, a Gallup poll.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.989
Said fifty six percent of Americans.

00:02:26.989 --> 00:02:34.430
Believed at that time that they were better
off than they were four years ago, despite

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.409
the fact that they had been in the pandemic.

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:40.110
They still believe that they were better off.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.659
That's a Trump thing.

00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:51.290
That's a Trump thing.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:03:00.659
And then Josh Holly gets a standing ovation
after reminding the crowd that he voted not

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:06.310
to certify the election results on January
6th, this was part of what incited the violent

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.880
riot.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.079
And the crowd gives Josh Holly a standing
ovation.

00:03:10.079 --> 00:03:15.950
You know, on January the 6th, I objected during
the Electoral College certification.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:25.930
Maybe you heard about it.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:26.930
I stood up.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:33.370
I guess the crowd believes that they are being
principled in some way by giving Josh Hawley

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:40.219
this standing ovation for an action, Hallie's
action, much like Ted Cruz and others that

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:45.109
melded with Rudy Giuliani's trial by combat
thing and all of this other stuff.

00:03:45.109 --> 00:03:49.200
And, of course, Trump's speech saying let's
go to the capital and led to a riot.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.300
The crowd cheering it.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:57.019
Then Matt Schlapp, who runs the American Conservative
Union, that's the organization that organizes

00:03:57.019 --> 00:04:04.819
CPAC, saying that what happened in November,
it was an unconstitutional power grab and

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:10.980
leaving CPAC, it would be do all you can to
any member that we have any influence over

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.290
to explain to them that it's unacceptable
to have this unconstitutional power grab on

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:22.200
elections so that what we saw this election
will be what you will see every single election.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.780
And we have to fight it now.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.790
It wasn't an unconstitutional power grab.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.970
It was that Joe Biden won.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:30.630
They still can't accept it.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.090
And why should they?

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:36.700
Trump still hasn't accepted that Hillary got
more votes than him in 2016.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.980
It's been five years and Trump doesn't accept
those results.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.970
So, of course, they're not going to accept
the results from almost four months ago.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:50.030
Since they think they won, they won't be changing
their strategy either.

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.630
And here's House minority leader.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:57.660
Gives me great pleasure to say, Minority Leader
Kevin McCarthy laying out the plan.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:58.860
Listen.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:02.250
We're going to continue to do exactly what
we did in the last election, OK?

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.560
I mean, if you think you won, I guess you
do the same thing.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.820
And they are also, as we talked about earlier
in the show, planning to suppress more votes.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.700
They're already scheming to do it.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:20.730
We gave you a report earlier in the show about
253 different bills and measures to suppress

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.350
voting across 43 states.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.040
Republicans believe they won.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:29.990
I guess certainly they don't want to change
their strategy, but they didn't suppress enough

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.490
votes and that's what they're going to try
to do now.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.370
